T4 CI matrix round 2 — platform-specific fixes beyond the mcp events
family (gh run 42158718976; branch b85-npm-tail). 2026-11-06.

== Leg 1: windows dir-fsync "Access is denied" x18 (PRODUCT-side) ==

Diagnosis: internal/mcp/manifest.go fsyncDir did os.Open(dir)+d.Sync().
On windows os.Open yields a read-only handle and Sync (FlushFileBuffers)
needs FILE_WRITE_DATA -> Access denied on every workspace durability
test (writeDurableFile -> fsyncDir at manifest.go:142; call sites:
manifest writes, ws_put driver writes - 18 tests).

Fix (commit "fix: skip dir-fsync on windows ..."): fsyncDir split into
  internal/mcp/fsync_unix.go     //go:build !windows  (unchanged body)
  internal/mcp/fsync_windows.go  //go:build windows   (no-op + why)
Windows has no POSIX dir-fsync; NTFS journals metadata and the file's
own fsync (writable handle - works on windows) persists data before
the rename; atomicity (no torn reads) is platform-independent. Standard
portable pattern (sqlite et al).

== Leg 2: windows TestResolveUSBDevice (test-side) ==

Diagnosis: the by-id fixture name carries MAC colons
(usb-Espressif_..._3C:0F:02:D7:58:84-if00) - colons are NTFS
alternate-data-stream separators, so os.Symlink fails "filename syntax
is incorrect" (before symlink privileges are even consulted). by-id
symlink trees are udev/unix device-manager semantics.
Fix: symlink leg moved to serial_unix_test.go (//go:build !windows);
portable legs (direct path as-is, unknown-name error naming both
candidates) stay in serial_test.go and run everywhere
(TestResolveUSBDeviceDirectAndUnknown).

== Leg 3: macos TestResolveUSBDevice /private/var (test-side) ==

Diagnosis: product resolveUSBDevice canonicalizes with
filepath.EvalSymlinks (correct); on darwin t.TempDir() is under
/var/folders (a symlink) so the resolved path gains /private and the
test's LITERAL comparison failed.
Fix: expected values canonicalized the same way (canonical() helper =
EvalSymlinks on the fixture tty path), both tests.

== Leg 4: windows+macos TestShortSockDirBindsLongNames 104-byte budget ==

Diagnosis (both directions of one stale constant):
  windows: check used flat sun_pathMax=104 and rejected a 105-byte path
           although windows AF_UNIX budget is 108 (afunix.h) - the
           helper itself was fine (os.TempDir() 38 bytes stayed).
  macos:   riskyBaseLen=80 never fired for /var/folders (~49 bytes) +
           the 46-byte probe name -> 117 > 104; threshold was tuned
           for short socket names, not the long-name contract.
Fix: internal/testutil/shortsock.go
  - sunPathBudget(): darwin 104 / linux 107 / windows 108
  - riskyBaseLen() = budget - dirCost(22) - nameAllowance(48):
    darwin 34 (catches /var/folders 49 -> /tmp fallback),
    linux 37 (/tmp=4 unaffected), windows 38 (CI %TEMP% 38 stays;
    38+1+20+1+46=106<=108).
  - shortsock_test.go: platform-budget check + new
    TestShortSockDirReservesNameAllowance (exactly-48-byte name must
    fit on every host).

